<title>PORTUGAL: BCP 1996 cons net up 14.8 pct to 23.268 bln esc.</title>
<headline>BCP 1996 cons net up 14.8 pct to 23.268 bln esc.</headline>
<dateline>LISBON 1997-01-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Jan 1 1996 to Dec 31 1996:</p>
<p>(billion escudos, unless stated)</p>
<p>Cons net  23.268 vs 20.273</p>
<p>Dividend 70 esc vs 65 esc (62.1 adjusted)</p>
<p>Financial margin 3.2 pct vs 2.9 pct</p>
<p>Loans 2,187.00 vs 1,997.0</p>
<p>Total assets 5,468.0 vs 5,404.00</p>
<p>Solvability ratio 9.3 pct vs 9.3 pct</p>
<p>Return on equity 12.0 pct vs 12.3 pct</p>
<p>Return on assets (before minorities) 0.9 pct vs 0.9 pct</p>
<p>Return on assets (after minorities) 0.4 pct vs 0.4 pct</p>
<p>Dividend payout 41.1 pct vs 35.1 pct</p>
<p>Dividend yield 3.4 pct vs 3.2 pct</p>
<p>Note - Results for 1995 and 1996 are not fully comparable because of the acquisition by Banco Comercial Portugues of another Portuguese bank, Banco Portugues do Atlantico, in 1995.</p>
<p>The 1995 dividend, adjusted for a dilution in the number of shares after a capital increase, was 62.1 escudos per share.</p>
<p>-- Lisbon newsroom +351-1-3538254</p>
</text>
